# udev rules example for ezcap raw-capture permissions
#
# The preferred setup runs ezcap-daemon as a systemd service with
# AmbientCapabilities=CAP_BPF CAP_NET_RAW CAP_PERFMON (see
# packaging/systemd/ezcap.service). This file documents the alternative
# for hosts where capabilities are managed via udev — e.g. running the
# daemon as a dedicated user that must open a packet socket.
#
# Install to /etc/udev/rules.d/99-ezcap.rules and reload with:
#   udevadm control --reload && udevadm trigger
#
# Grant the packet socket capability to the dedicated ezcap user for
# network interface capture. Adjust INTERFACE or the GROUP to match the
# deployment.
#
# SUBSYSTEM=="net", ACTION=="add", KERNEL=="eth0", \\
#   RUN+="/sbin/setcap cap_net_raw+ep /usr/bin/ezcap-daemon"
#
# NOTE: setcap grants the *binary* the capability for every invocation.
# Prefer the systemd AmbientCapabilities route when available — it scopes
# the privilege to the service unit only. This example is provided for
# completeness on systems without that option.
